     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the maximum labeled daily dose. Single doses above 800 mg add no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit but raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. I can't think of an indication where this would be a safe dose, and I don't want to put it into the system as a routine order.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a note to monitor renal function and watch for GI bleeding.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), if that's enough for the clinical goal.\n\nIf you need more effect than that, I can help with a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen, or with another agent.\n\nIf you still want the 6,400 mg/day dose, it would need to go through direct entry and pharmacist review. That way a second clinician checks it, and I'm not the one entering it."
      }
